{
  "description": "Tool annotations and the approval path. Pins Rust approval_hint_for / McpPool::record_tool_approval_hints through McpPool::to_api_tools: a server-declared destructiveHint makes the tool Destructive (each call keeps its prompt), but a readOnlyHint on an ordinary (non-reviewed-plugin) server relaxes nothing: annotations are claims, not proof. destructiveHint wins over readOnlyHint. The trusted-read-only hint needs a reviewed plugin and is not reachable from a transcript.",
  "server_name": "conformance",
